// ============================================================
// TODO BACKLOG — Core Framework Tasks
// Process: STRICT HOLD — do NOT implement any task until the
// backlog is declared complete. Then pick ONLY the first
// uncompleted task, implement it, write validation tests,
// mark it [x] here, and stop for review.
// ============================================================

// Phase 0: AI Coding Agent
// [x] 0. AI coding agent (Claude Code / Codex style): Add an autonomous "Agent" mode to the AI panel (toggle + Ctrl+Shift+A). PerchAgent receives a task in natural language, explores the whole workspace (list/read), plans and makes multi-file edits directly to the virtual file tree, runs .js files to verify its own changes, and iterates until done — all via a bounded generateText tool-call loop (max 15 calls, Stop button). Every agent write is snapshotted (revertible from the Timeline or a per-write Revert button) and marks the file dirty.

// Phase 1: Editor & Code Quality
// [x] 1. More languages: Enable syntax highlighting for Python, JSON, CSS, Markdown, and TypeScript in addition to the existing JavaScript. Language auto-detects from file extension, with a manual override in the status bar or command palette.
// [x] 2. Live preview pane: Add a toggleable split-view render pane. When the active file is .html or .md, render it live (debounced ~300ms after typing stops): HTML in a sandboxed iframe, Markdown as styled HTML. Show a clear placeholder for non-previewable files.
// [x] 3. Multi-cursor editing: Enable multi-cursor editing: Ctrl+D selects the next occurrence of the current selection; Ctrl+Alt+Up/Down adds a cursor on the line above/below. Each cursor edits independently; ESC collapses to a single cursor.
// [x] 4. Autocomplete + snippets: Provide built-in completions for JavaScript, HTML, and CSS (keywords, identifiers, common snippets) with Tab to accept. Support user-editable snippet files (JSON snippet definitions) that add to the built-ins; Tab cycles through snippet placeholders.
// [x] 5. Code folding: Allow collapsing/expanding of function bodies, braces, and block comments via gutter indicators and shortcuts (Ctrl+Shift+[ / Ctrl+Shift+]). Fold state persists per file for the current session.
// [x] 6. Minimap: Add a right-edge scroll preview rendering a scaled (1-2px per line) block view of the whole file with the current viewport highlighted; clicking or dragging it scrolls the editor. Toggleable.
// [x] 7. Linter/diagnostics panel: Detect JavaScript syntax errors live as you type (debounced ~400ms) and surface them in a Problems panel grouped by file with line numbers and messages, plus a badge count on the tab; clicking an entry jumps to the line. Show error markers in the editor gutter/line.
// [x] 8. Find & replace with regex: Implement Find in the active file (match highlighting, next/prev, replace one/all) and Find in Workspace across all files (results grouped by file with match counts; click to jump). Regex mode toggle applies to both.
// [x] 9. AI code assistant: Add a chat panel powered by generateText that can explain, fix, or generate code and propose edits to the open file as a diff the user can apply or reject. Stream responses with an animated loading indicator.
// [x] 10. Git-style version history: Snapshot every file on save (kv-backed, keyed per file). Provide a timeline to browse past versions, restore any snapshot, and diff any snapshot against the current content in a side-by-side view. Keep a per-file cap (e.g. 50 snapshots) to bound storage.

// Phase 2: Files & Workspace
// [x] 11. Import/export zip: Add download of the entire workspace as a single .zip and upload of a .zip to restore it (extract files and folders, merging with existing content). Report clear errors for malformed archives.
// [x] 12. Share via link: Serialize the workspace into a shareable URL (compressed); for workspaces too large for a URL, use an editable upload and embed its URL. Anyone opening the link sees the workspace restored (read-only).
// [x] 13. Drag & drop: Support dragging files and folders in the file tree to reorder them within a folder or move them into another folder (drop targets highlight). Also support dragging a file's reordering inside its current folder.
// [x] 14. Duplicate file & terminal expansion: Add "Duplicate" to the file context menu (creates "<name> copy.ext" in the same folder). Expand the terminal command set beyond the current 13 with cp, mv, grep, find, head, and tail supporting common flags, matching the existing command UX.
// [x] 15. Compare files: Add a side-by-side diff view comparing two open files: choose the second file from the tree, then show added/removed/changed line highlighting with navigation between differences.

// Phase 3: Perchance Integration
// [x] 16. Edit your own generator: Add a one-click button that loads this generator's real main.pjs and index.html into the editor as editable files (scratchpad mode). Saving edits writes them back to the live generator; show an explicit indicator of edit/save state. [Implemented as a guided-publish scratchpad: Perchance exposes no save API from the output iframe (session cookie is required on perchance.org), so after editing you Publish… → Copy a file → paste it into the Perchance editor and Save. The scratchbar shows ● edited / ✓ published / · unchanged per file, with Reload live (re-fetch) and Exit.]

// Phase 3.5: AI Providers
// [x] 21. Bring-your-own-key AI providers: Settings gains an AI section with a provider choice (Perchance free / OpenAI / OpenRouter / Microsoft Foundry / Hugging Face / custom OpenAI-compatible URL), a model field, and a masked API-key field stored only in the user's browser. The AI assistant and PerchAgent route through a unified aiComplete() layer: Perchance uses generateText; the rest call the provider's OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions via super-fetch (streaming SSE where available). Falls back to Perchance when no key is set.
// [x] 22. Model picker: The AI panel header shows a dropdown of preset models for the active provider (plus the current custom model and an "Edit models…" shortcut to Settings). Changing it updates the saved config and applies to both Chat and Agent modes.

// Phase 4: UI & Polish
// [x] 17. Split editors: Support side-by-side editors ("Split Right") for two files: an adjustable divider, independent cursors and undo per pane, and the ability to close a split.
// [x] 18. Breadcrumbs: Show a path trail (folder/file chain) above the editor that follows the active file; clicking any segment jumps to that file or folder.
// [x] 19. More themes: Add light and high-contrast presets alongside the existing dark theme, plus an accent color picker. The theme affects editor chrome and syntax colors and persists across sessions.
// [x] 20. Custom keybindings: Add an editable keybindings.json that remaps command-palette actions; ship the default bindings as a reference and let user overrides take precedence over defaults.

$meta
  title = PerchEdit — Code Editor in Your Browser
  description = A code editor that runs entirely in your browser: virtual file tree, syntax highlighting, a terminal, command palette, search, and a JavaScript runner. Your files persist across reloads.
  tags = code editor, perchance, terminal, javascript, tools
  header
    mode = minimal

kv = {import:kv-plugin}
generateText = {import:ai-text-plugin}
uploadPlugin = {import:upload-plugin}
superFetch = {import:super-fetch-plugin}

config
  appName = Code
